  "rdma_flowtags": {
    "comment": "per-(src,dst) PCC flowtags, probed via 0xdea 2026-07-11; sgpu03/sgpu04 added 2026-08-23. The tag hashes (src function, dst function) and is stable across QP recreation, IP choice and reflash. KNOWN COLLISION: src vf1 and src vf2 produce identical tags for every dst (rows below are equal), so vf1->X and vf2->X RDMA budgets are inseparable at the RP - never schedule both concurrently. tx_agent_e keys RDMA budgets by 'src>dst' with fallback to the per-vnic flowtag.  CARD-INDEPENDENT (2026-08-23): sgpu03 and sgpu04 return the same tag as sgpu01 for all four straight pairs, so the hash reads the function INDEX, not the card. Each sender DPU runs its own RP, so identical tags on different senders are not a collision. The vf1/vf2 SOURCE collision noted above is a property of the index hash and therefore applies to every sender node alike. The sgpu03/sgpu04 cross-pair rows were carried over from that argument and then CHECKED: vf0>vf1, vf3>vf0, vf1>vf3 and vf2>vf1 probed on sgpu03 all came back equal to the sgpu01 rows. Probing a cross pair needs the NON-CM path (-x <gid>, not -R): with rdma_cm the kernel picks the source VF from the destination subnet, the flow is really a straight pair, and the tag read back is the destination's own - which is what three of four first readings were before the method was fixed.",
