  "policy": {
    "comment": "design_v4.md §2. VM == vnic in this lab. weight = W_i (inter-tenant); max_rate_bps = MaxRate_i (null = uncapped); class_weights = W_{i,TCP}/W_{i,RDMA}. per_sender_weights: 'dst_vnic|class|src_vnic' -> u (absent = 1). LAB SHAPE 2026-08-26: every host carries 8 VFs and every VF is sold at 50 Gb/s, enforced by two class-blind layers that do not know about each other (tools/lab-infra/vf_caps.sh): devlink tx_max on the VF's representor at its own DPU (uplink), and an OVS drop-band meter on traffic addressed to the VF at its own DPU (downlink, a naive cloud policer: drops excess, marks nothing). HPFT reads the same number as MaxRate. 8 VMs x 50G = 400G > C' so the ROOT layer binds under full load; one VM alone stays capped below the 200G link.",
