  "e_params": {
    "comment": "design_v4.md: the fence law. The receiver keeps a virtual-queue ledger per flow-set (Q <- clip(Q + A - E, 0, D*E)) and sends only q = Q/E; the sender steps the fence multiplicatively R <- R*exp(alpha*min(m,m_max))*exp(-kappa*dq)*exp(-(kappa/D)*min(q,D)). Every constant below is per-feedback and dimensionless, so none of them change with link rate or flow count - see design_theory_v4.md §5 (scale invariance) and §6, which derives kappa, D and alpha_max from just two measurements (period T_p, loop delay tau) and two dimensionless choices (damping zeta, overshoot budget epsilon). HEADROOM=0.08: ~3% queue-warning margin plus the ~5% VxLAN encap tax (inner-byte ledger vs outer-byte wire, measured 4.99% at 1500 MTU).",
